  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SAWA II- Enhance Resilience for Micro- businesses and Create Sustainable livelihood Opportunities in the Gaza Strip (phase II)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;b&gt;The EU funded &lt;/b&gt;SAWA II project&amp;nbsp;brings together institutions, communities, and entrepreneurs around a common goal: to create meaningful, lasting change by supporting inclusive economic growth and sustainable development, particularly in times of crisis. &lt;br&gt;SAWA II aims at enhancing economic resilience by enhancing the competitiveness and sustainability of Micro and Small Enterprises (MSEs) in the West Bank and Gaza Strip. The project aims to contribute to this through focusing on the competitiveness of the private sector through designing and implementing tailor-made business development services with a particular focus on the green and circular economy as an opportunity to improve businesses performance. Additionally, SAWA II is an opportunity to strengthen financial sustainability by providing continuity of support both in terms of technical and financial support and facilitating access to alternative sources of finance.</narrative>
  </description>
